# Publishing the design documents

The Functional Design Document and Technical Design Document are Google Docs. Update them from a local `.docx` in two commands. Do not invent another upload path.

```bash
python3 scripts/stage-design-docx.py path/to/the.docx
python3 scripts/check-design-doc.py FILE_ID path/to/the.docx
```

`stage-design-docx.py` prints one https URL. Pass that URL to `google_drive-update-file` as `filePath`, with `keepRevisionForever` true. Leave `mimeType` unset.

- FDD file id: `1PoeiXKR2twOaz_JcRN0e4ZQkUCuDD5qnnyrlt6ygkeU`
- TDD file id: `1K6-ghhSnJZcrch81DDhmHXXYU0pSF7tOGR9S9jiCUjk`

Run the check after the update. Reply with the new first line only after it exits 0.

Leave the file bytes on disk. Do not paste the `.docx`, its base64, or a data URL into a tool call. Do not send it through assistant storage. Do not create a second Google Doc. Do not put the staging URL in the reply.

If the Drive file description still names the previous documentation version, set `description` in a second `google_drive-update-file` call that has no `filePath`.
